Package: lrcm
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Florian Gusinde <florian.gusinde@72it.de>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-git, python3-ansible-runner, python3-jinja2, python3-validators, python3-distro, git, cron | cron-daemon
Homepage: https://lrcm.72it.de
Description: agent for Linux remote configuration management
 lrcm clones a git repository containing Ansible playbooks and applies them to
 the local machine. It targets Linux clients that cannot be reached from a
 central management infrastructure: remote schools and universities, IoT
 devices, unattended terminals, marketing displays and sensors.
 .
 The agent has a very small memory and CPU footprint, serialises itself with a
 pidfile lock, staggers its start with a randomised delay and can install and
 remove its own cron entries.
